== Reward ==

* [[Chapter IV, Of Flame and Frost]]
* [[Holiday Gift]]

== Walkthrough ==

You say, 'Hail, Frosti Bramblebrew'

: Frosti Bramblebrew says, 'Ah! You don't have the look of a snow-skulker. No, you've got warm fingers and colder feet — just the sort I need! See, I'm working on a new recipe — gloves that warm the hands and the heart. Meant to honor a tradition nearly lost — one the Elves used to call the [Emberfold Exchange].'

You say, 'What Emberfold Exchange'

: Frosti Bramblebrew says, 'A ritual from when flame and frost weren't enemies. Long before the wars, when warmth was a gift, not a weapon. Each year, an Elf would craft a pair of enchanted mittens, made from both frost-hide and emberberries. One was kept; the other, given to someone in need — even an enemy. The Icestar loved that. It glowed brightest when kindness crossed the coldest lines. Now… I just need the [ingredients].'

You say, 'What ingredients'

: Frosti Bramblebrew says, 'Frostbitten Hide, from frozen mammoths, Emberberry Cluster, found in the lair of fire dragons, and the Dew of First Light, dropped by wisps of magical energy.'

: Frosti Bramblebrew wipes berry juice from his sleeve and shrugs.

You will need the following:

* [[Frostbitten Hide]] from any mammoth in [[Everfrost Peaks]]
* [[Emberberry Cluster]] from any goblins in [[Solusek's Eye]]
* [[Dew of First Light]] from any willowisp.

Upon turning all three into Frosti Bramblebrew, he will say...

: Frosti Bramblebrew stirs the pot, then pulls free a pair of soft, glowing mittens. A single page shimmers inside one of them, he says, 'Oho! You’ve done it. Even got the dew just right — not too sparkly, not too shy. What’s this? Hiding where it’s warmest. Clever page. Go on then — back to the preamble with you!'

You receive [[Chapter IV, Of Flame and Frost]] and a [[Holiday Gift]].

